# d3-check rule
- Reuse first: search d3utils/timers/controller/pycore; extend, never reimplement or duplicate constants/helpers.
- Import `pycore.*` directly; no `providor.common_imports` wrapper. Literals → `providor.app_constants`; structured → `config`. i18n only via `providor.i18n_manager`.
- `share/values` = data only, `share/common` = shared funcs/base; no run_/do_, no data/store/cache dirs. One-shot via `timers.timer_manager.submit_one_shot` + `one_shot_tasks.do_*`.
- Threads: event center only, init at startup, native Thread, no mutual blocking.
- Flow on/off + per-step/node state owned ONLY by `d3utils.rosbot_flow*`; controller/timers/UI are third-party callers (call public flow fns, never read/write flow state). Tick entry `rosbot_task_processor.process_task()` reads `rosbot_flow_state` + calls `tick_bn_only_flow()`/`tick_flow_master()`.
- No defensive runtime API detection (`hasattr`/`callable`/`getattr(...,None)`); call by contract. Imports at file top (only exception: optional third-party `try/except ImportError`); fix cycles by architecture, not lazy import.
- Drop unnecessary try/except; keep only websocket/network, task threads, Tk lifecycle, queue, COM/OS, signal handlers.
- Code/comments/logs in English; user-facing strings via i18n.
- New standards → `.cursor/rules`, `.cursor/skills`, `AGENTS.md`; d3-check prompts → `pyapps/d3-check/.prompts/`.
